course: dictionary
lesson: 15990
title: Utility: services and usefulness
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning, so look at the words around it to find the right one. «Our utility bills went up this winter.» Bills are things you pay for, so here a utility is a service such as gas or electricity.
explain: «The washing machine is in the utility room.» A utility room is a room for practical jobs like washing and drying clothes. Here utility describes the room. Try the swap test: put "useful" in place of "utility" and check that the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Utility can also mean usefulness, which is a more formal word. «The tool has great utility on a farm» means the tool is very useful. The same word can do three different jobs, so always check the context.
fact: A utility is a service that people need in their homes, such as water, gas or electricity.
fact: «Utility bills» are the payments people make for water, gas and electricity.
fact: Utility means usefulness, and it is a formal word.
fact: As an adjective, utility describes something practical and useful, like «a utility room».
fact: In computers, a utility is a small useful program.
exercise: «Our utility bills went up this winter.» What are utility bills? | Letters from school about homework | Bills for buying new clothes | *Payments for things like water, gas and electricity
exercise: «The washing machine is in the utility room.» What is a utility room used for? | Watching films and playing games | Sleeping and resting | *Useful jobs such as washing and drying clothes
exercise: «The tool has great utility on a farm.» What does utility mean here? | *Usefulness | Price | Colour | Length
test: In a computer, what is a utility? | A kind of keyboard | A game with levels | *A small useful program | A type of printer
test: Which sentence uses utility as an adjective, describing something? | The utilities were cut off in the storm | Our utility bills arrived today | Utility means being useful | *The utility van carried pipes to the building site
exam: Which word names a service like water, gas or electricity that homes need? | Furniture | Vehicle | *Utility | Sunshine
